+ * read in [-1,1] (NV divides by 127, snorm does too), so the alias is exact. The 8/16-bit
+ * distinction is not kept: Mesa picks the size. One concession:
+ * GL_SIGNED_RGB8_UNSIGNED_ALPHA8_NV mixes signed and unsigned and has no snorm twin, so the
+ * whole texel ends up signed.
