+/*
+ * Support for the legacy NVIDIA OpenGL extensions that Mesa implements in the
+ * core (i.e. driver independently): GL_NV_fence, GL_NV_occlusion_query,
+ * GL_NV_register_combiners, GL_NV_register_combiners2,
+ * GL_NV_pixel_data_range, GL_NV_vertex_array_range, GL_NV_point_sprite.
+ *
+ * The entry points here are thin layers on top of equivalent core/ARB
+ * machinery, so that they work on every driver (including zink) without any
+ * backend support.
+ *
+ * Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
+ * copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"),
+ * to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation
+ * on the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
+ * subllise, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to
+ * whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following
+ * conditions:
+ *
+ * The above copyright notice and this permission notice (including the next
+ * paragraph) shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the
+ * Software.
+ *
+ * THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
