+/* nv-legacy: MESA_NV_SHADOW_CLAMP=<0|1> also protects the ARB non-projective shadow
+ * reference. The NV model clamps the reference before comparing; Mad Mod Mike's target6
+ * planar shadow has coordinates whose third component can leave [0,1] when the point is
+ * outside the shadow map. Without the clamp the comparison fails and the polygon becomes a
+ * hard shadow; with it the outside-map region stays lit, as on the real 9800. On by default.
+ */
+bool
+_mesa_nv_shadow_clamp_enabled(void)
