+struct translate_state {
+   /* nvlegacy: Cg records the initial value of a program's named parameters in the
+    * comment block, not in an instruction: "#var <type> <name> : ... : c[<slot>] : ..."
+    * says which constant register the name lives in, and "#default <name> = v ..." gives
+    * the value. The reference driver applied them at load time. Measured on Mad Mod Mike
+    * (2026-11-09): its composite/fullscreen vertex program reads x0y0x1y1 (c[2]),
+    * y_limits, quadrant, dest_texsize and blur_texel_radius, the application never writes
+    * a single parameter on a vertex program (the reference trace has 58167 calls to
+    * glProgramLocalParameter4dvARB, all of them GL_FRAGMENT_PROGRAM_ARB, and zero on
+    * GL_VERTEX_PROGRAM_ARB), and the program text has no DECLARE section (2030 bytes in
+    * both the reference and ours, zero DECLARE lines in both). So without the comments the
+    * constants stay zero: the composite draws a degenerate rectangle over a cleared
+    * framebuffer and the frame comes out black (luminance 0,023 against 0,176 with the
+    * pass replaced, and in our captured sequence 8 frames out of 24 are at 0,012 with the
+    * menu button and the NVIDIA logo still drawn, while the reference video has 6 samples
+    * out of 272 that dark and they are the loading window and the closing fades). */
